# vehje-signature. language definition

The framework's language-level definition, split from the per-program
`vehje-ir`: the graded algebraic signature (families as operations of an
algebraic-effect theory, each with its effect grade and per-operand coeffect
discipline, the attribute-grammar attachment point, the lease-rule schema, and
the declared target set) and its three projections (the eliminator IR, the
introduction value domain, the introduction-compiled stencils). Data only; the
compilation over it is `vehje-runtime-gen`'s. `vehje-ir` is what a program is,
`vehje-signature` is what a language is. `#![no_std]`, no alloc.
